ecord refusal and previously established predecessor/reducer/enum behavior. Do not repeat unrelated closed audits without new evidence. Shared API caller boundary is accepted; do not shrink remaining assigned requirements.\nCheck final-source provenance and actual exits for new narrowing mutants and same-instrument applied survivor; NOT_APPLIED/compile failure are not behavioral kills. Corrected formatting evidence must use existing paths. Reuse trustworthy exact-source prior evidence with explicit bounds; run necessary new independent regressions. All CI is local. Never edit the active product candidate or integrate; attach task-scoped verdict and raw evidence, then route accept_cr or changes requested through the normal lifecycle.\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev6.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev6.md`\n\n- Byte count: `2183`\n- Content digest: `sha256:f366940896a06c99b9d895b6cc9df27d63619f290c91fdc65471b7b79a4d0449`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-21gygk_reviewer-after-rev6.md\nIndependently review the newly published candidate after CR6. Read CR6 verdict/evidence, producer outcome and required clause-to-owner conformance matrix. Verify checkpoint persistence against actual Session.kind for winner and necessary ancestry with positive direct/task_board and wrong-variant controls through BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate and both summaries. Verify N-chain-self compiles and reaches its intended admission violation on exact final source; inspect affected shipped plants plus applied harmless survivor with real exit evidence.\nThe repeated authority family requires checking the matrix against actual APIs and pinned5.3/5.4/14.7.2, distinguishing canonical shape, related-record semantics and accepted caller/publication responsibilities. Do not accept claimed delegation if the owner lacks required input. Retain closed ancestry/creator, canonical identit