{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c41f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0892e-c94e-7771-b9cd-b99166499f5d"},"sequence":106,"recorded_at":1780531400000207,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0892f059b7b53ae7c21b418042fc4","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_rework-rev7.md`.\n1|Rework CR7 without reducing scope. Read review-verdict-rev7.md and evidence. Port TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority first, retaining passing real event controls and reproducing missing/later-lease failures. CR6 persistence and self-link mutation findings are CLOSED; do not re-litigate prior closed ancestry/creator/canonical/lagging/parked/capability/predecessor gates.\n2|The failed class audit is C6: checkpoint event authority was delegated to APIs that lack event repositories/closure inputs. Implement actual shared admission of required checkpoint event-head closure against Session/Lease relationships for winner AND every necessary ancestor, used by BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate and both summaries. Preserve valid historical heads, not equality with current tails; preserve branching/lagging. Missing references, unavailable source reads, cross-session or later/losing-lease facts must be distinguished per pinned contracts. Use existing production repository/attestation/reducer boundaries as appropriate; no synthetic digest placeholders or caller-trusted validation claims.\n3|Read the entire pinned5.4 checkpoint-consumer event/profile paragraph and2.4 profile requirements, then make C6 complete for this owned admission path. The reviewer only demonstrated missing/later-lease heads and explicitly did not prove profile scenarios; that is not permission to leave a known owned profile relationship unchecked. Add production-entry evidence for every owned closure/profile relationship or identify a REAL implementing API with required inputs and executable witness. Do not invent an external/human blocker or invoke generic publication-owner prose. Caller-owned storage/publication/transport/CLI effects remain outside scope and must not be implemented gratuitously.\n4|Correct conformance matrix C6 and its false delegation conclusion. Verify other matrix delegations by actual input/call/test evidence before handoff. Add a qualifying narrowing invalid-reference plant and same-instrument applied harmless survivor; run affected existing plants on final source so signature changes cannot leave compiling evidence stale. Preserve8-row AC denominator and precise limits, all local required validation, bytes restored after mutations. No hosted CI, manual commits/integration, broad Git restore/clean, scratch admission or extra sibling writer. Normal task-board handoff only after complete rework/evidence.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c421","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0892e-c94e-7771-b9cd-b99166499f5d"},"sequence":107,"recorded_at":1780531400000209,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0892f06367d20ae6588b82d0f3723","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev7.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — CR7: changes requested\n2|\n3|Reviewed immutable candidate tree `0715659e5ac515b387a9a3e5926cba4138d9cbea`, base `8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`, Story checkpoint `83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`. Authority: AX v0.6.0, `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`. All 49 changed paths match both the exact archive and active candidate by bytes. No active product, index, branch or commit was modified. All CI is local.\n4|\n5|## P1 — Checkpoint event-head authority is never admitted\n6|\n7|repeat-of: CR5/CR6 canonical-identity-versus-related-record-authority family. This is the C6 relationship explicitly included in the CR6 rework audit, not reopening the repaired ancestry, creator or persistence gates.\n8|\n9|`internal/sessquery/lease.go:191-245` attests the canonical Checkpoint Record but never extracts or resolves `event_heads`. `checkWinnerCheckpoint` (`lease.go:392`) and `checkCheckpointBinding` (`lease.go:481`) admit a required checkpoint after checking session, lease, creator and persistence variant. Neither establishes the checkpoint's event authority. `Revalidate` uses those same gates at `revalidate.go:101`; `collectAuthorityHeads` (`revalidate.go:257`) binds the winning Lease Record and present source tails, not the required checkpoint's closure.\n10|\n11|Pinned Section 5.3 requires a validated checkpoint for every necessary successor link. Section 5.4 defines checkpoint event_heads as the authoritative DAG immediately before that object and specifies closure/profile-reference integrity. Section 14.7.2 requires a validated winning Lease Record and current complete authority. A canonical checkpoint naming an absent event or an event under a later lease cannot establish that authority.\n12|\n13|Independent `TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority` proves the omission through production calls:\n14|\n15|- Both controls PASS. They create actual local Session Events, reach idle under the owning lease, bind the checkpoint to that actual head, and use canonical Lease/Checkpoint Records with correct session, epoch, holder and direct persistence variant.\n16|- Both winner negatives FAIL: replacing only checkpoint event_heads with a missing digest or an existing later-lease event is admitted by `Reader.BuildPlan`, freshly built plan `Reader.Revalidate`, `Reader.AuthoritativeStatus` and `Reader.AuthoritativeList`.\n17|- Both necessary-ancestor negatives FAIL through those same entries. Additionally, `Reader.Revalidate(oldPlan)` returns nil after changing only the ancestor checkpoint's heads and its canonical referring ancestor Lease Record. The winning Lease Record, session and event bytes remain unchanged.\n18|- Old-plan winner changes correctly refuse because the winner's digest changes. This is retained behavior, not evidence that checkpoint closure was checked.\n19|\n20|Final `probes.log`: exit 1, four invalid-head subtests fail, both head controls pass. The same invocation also passes all eight independent direct/task_board persistence controls/negatives. Earlier invalid test setup/control attempts are preserved and excluded explicitly.\n21|\n22|Reproduce from an archive of CR7: copy attached `reviewer_rev7_test.go` into `internal/sessquery/`, then run:\n23|\n24|```sh\n25|go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev7' -count=1 -v\n26|```\n27|\n28|Fix the shared admission of event authority for every checkpoint required by the winning ancestry. Preserve valid historical checkpoint heads rather than requiring them to equal today's tail; preserve valid branching/lagging copies. Distinguish a proved missing reference from an unavailable read and propagate required-source failures. Add focused production negatives and a narrowing mutant that admits one invalid reference, with an applied harmless survivor through the same instrument.\n29|\n30|This finding does not demand manifest publication, storage, transport, CLI effect execution or a new recovery protocol. The fixture retains those accepted caller boundaries. It concerns the event/lease relationship of a checkpoint that this shared API already consumes to declare a lease validated.\n31|\n32|## The required conformance matrix is not yet a trustworthy closure claim\n33|\n34|The attached matrix's C5 delegation is substantiated: `canonicaljson.validateSafeBoundaryEvidence` reads the supplied safe-boundary members and rejects false booleans/nonzero counters, while the checkpoint validator enforces status and shape. C4 now has the necessary Session.kind input and its own shared gate.\n35|\n36|C6 instead names a generic checkpoint consumer/publication owner, and the final paragraph claims delegated APIs carry the needed inputs. There is no named implementation or test for that claim. `sessrepo.AttestCheckpointRecord(raw)` (`internal/sessrepo/checkpoint.go:22`) calls canonical identity validation; `canonicaljson.validateCheckpointRecord` (`core_records.go:147-153`) checks only the head array's cardinality, sorted uniqueness and digest syntax, without repositories or event closure. `provhost.ProfileMapping(providerID, profile)` only maps strings to adapter flags. The sessstate documentation explicitly excludes persisted-profile derivation and treats profile events as inert facts. None establishes C6 at the selector admission path.\n37|\n38|Correct C6 and the audit conclusion using real call sites/input contracts and behavioral evidence. Effective-profile consumer behavior itself was not newly exercised here; no claim is made that every profile scenario fails. The concrete missing/later-lease checkpoint-head admission above is sufficient to withhold acceptance. Do not turn the unsupported delegation into a scope exemption.\n39|\n40|## CR6 findings closed; retained conclusions\n41|\n42|- CR6 P1 is closed. Independent `TestRev7IndependentPersistence` covers direct AND task_board, winner AND necessary ancestry, valid controls AND wrong variants, BuildPlan, old-plan Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList. All eight subtests pass. The shipped TestRev6 suite also passes in the full exact-candidate run.\n43|- CR6 P2 is closed. The repaired `N-chain-self` compiles and is behaviorally KILLED by `TestSelfPredecessorWithCheckpointMustRefuse` on exact final source. It is no longer a compilation failure.\n44|- Closed ancestry/creator, canonical identity, lagging-copy, parked-source, seven-capability, changed-record, predecessor/reducer/enum and creation-crash findings remain closed. The full candidate suite was rerun, but unrelated historical mutation audits were not repeated wholesale.\n45|- Caller-owned CLI invocation, wire output/exit mapping, serialized effects and durable recovery remain accepted bounds. No public CLI behavior is credited to this library leaf.\n46|\n47|## AC coverage\n48|\n49|**8 of 8 AC rows driven through shared production entries; 4 of 8 established and 4 of 8 partial/failing.** Public CLI integration remains a stated bound: 0 of 8 CLI rows delivered here.\n50|\n51|| Row | Production call site and named candidate evidence | Review result |\n52|| --- | --- | --- |\n53|| UUID/name | Reader.Resolve; TestResolvePinnedPrecedence, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established |\n54|| Qualified selector | Reader.Resolve / resolveExplicit; TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex, TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures | Established |\n55|| Ambiguity | Reader.Resolve / matchName / checkRecordAgreement; TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established |\n56|| List summaries | Reader.AuthoritativeList / authorize / winningLeaseFor; TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals, TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole, TestAuthoritativeAdmitsFullCapabilityRegistry | Partial: P1 |\n57|| Status summaries | Reader.AuthoritativeStatus / authorize / winningLeaseFor; TestAuthoritativeStatusHealthy, TestAuthoritativeMissingProcessRefusesStatus, TestAuthoritativeHostNameBound64 | Partial: P1 |\n58|| Stable sorting | Reader.List / Resolve; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity | Established |\n59|| SelectionPlan | Reader.BuildPlan / Revalidate / ParsePlan; TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts, TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestValidSuccessorBuildsAndRevalidates, TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyRefuses, TestRev5*, TestRev6* | Partial: P1 |\n60|| Negative/refusal | Resolve / List / Status / BuildPlan / Revalidate; shipped refusal suites and mutation instrument, independent TestRev7CheckpointHeadAuthority | Partial: P1 |\n61|\n62|Reviewer TestRev7 is attached evidence, not part of the immutable candidate. Port it during rework; do not claim it is already shipped.\n63|\n64|## Validation and provenance\n65|\n66|Go library, darwin/arm64, Go 1.25.5. Required skills read, including main checkout's Curator-managed Go skill (managed links absent from this worktree). No installation, hosted CI or integration.\n67|\n68|Independent exact-source checks: full `go test ./... -count=1 -v`, coverage, `go build ./...`, full `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l internal` and exact-tree `git diff --check`. Actual final exits are recorded in `actual-exits.json`; gofmt used an existing path and listed no files. The reviewer probe is intentionally failing and remains exit 1.\n69|\n70|Independent focused mutation driver retains the shipped run() implementation and plants, filtering only the selection and setting the exact archive root: N-chain-self and N-checkpoint-persistence KILLED; applied C-harmless-comment SURVIVED; controls before/after pass. Each log records named failures and real subprocess exits. The five other affected lease plants are accepted from producer batch B: all five KILLED, controls pass. All internal bytes in producer batches A/B match this final candidate, verified in source-comparison.json; raw logs/manifests are copied into this review bundle. NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE controls are classified separately and never counted as kills. No full historical battery rerun is claimed.\n71|\n72|The evidence bundle contains candidate hashes, exact CR6-to-CR7 path list, original CR6 verdict/probe, producer outcome/matrix, publication log, new executable regressions, raw tests/checks/mutants and operational corrections. The task note records this review finding as the review logbook entry while product LOGBOOK stays untouched.\n73|\n74|Verdict: changes requested. Route to-dev; not blocked, accepted, integrating or done.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c423","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0892e-c94e-7771-b9cd-b99166499f5d"},"sequence":108,"recorded_at":1780531400000211,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0892f070978439c28a2bf64b94c24","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev6.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — CR6: changes requested\n2|\n3|Reviewed immutable tree `e8783471325b552f7057eda36c768102b34807d9`, base `8cf4aaaa190e6a11dff2661aa6806ce476128653`, Story checkpoint `83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`. Authority remains AX v0.6.0 at `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`. All 48 changed paths match the live candidate and the review archive by bytes; no board or stray mutation tree is in the immutable delta. No active product file, index, branch or commit was changed by this reviewer.\n4|\n5|## P1 — Checkpoint persistence variant is not bound to the Session Record\n6|\n7|repeat-of: CR5 semantic authority admission family (canonical identity mistaken for complete related-record validation); this is a new relationship, not reopening the repaired ancestor/holder findings.\n8|\n9|Pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md` Section 5.4 requires a direct Session Record's checkpoint to have non-null `provider_manifest_id` and null `task_board_bundle_id`; task_board requires the reverse. Section 5.3 requires validated checkpoints throughout necessary lease ancestry, and 14.7.2 requires validated current authority.\n10|\n11|`internal/sessquery/lease.go:195-229` attests canonical checkpoint shape/identity and extracts session/lease/creator, but does not bind the persistence variant to the Session Record. `checkWinnerCheckpoint` and `checkCheckpointBinding` (`lease.go:454-468`) never inspect that relationship. The canonical owner at `internal/canonicaljson/core_records.go:163-176` proves only exactly one persistence ID exists. Its no-Session-Record API cannot establish which variant is valid.\n12|\n13|Independent `TestRev6CheckpointPersistenceMustMatchSession` uses the existing valid direct-session fixture, canonical checkpoint identity, correct session, lease, epoch and creator. It swaps only provider/non-provider persistence fields, re-identifies the checkpoint and updates the referencing lease digest. Both positive direct controls PASS; both invalid variant subtests FAIL with exit 1:\n14|\n15|- Winning-successor case: BuildPlan succeeds, Revalidate of that plan returns nil, and AuthoritativeStatus and AuthoritativeList succeed.\n16|- Necessary-ancestor case: all the same entries succeed. Additionally, an originally valid plan remains accepted by Revalidate after changing only the ancestor's checkpoint variant and canonical referencing lease. The winner record and event bytes remain unchanged.\n17|\n18|Raw evidence: `probes.log`, executable `reviewer_rev6_executed_test.go`. Reproduce by copying this reviewer test into the exact candidate's `internal/sessquery/` in scratch and running `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev6CheckpointPersistenceMustMatchSession$' -count=1 -v`.\n19|\n20|Fix the shared semantic admission path for every checkpoint required by the winning ancestry, using the actual Session Record kind. Add positive direct/task_board controls and wrong-variant negatives, including old-plan revalidation, through all four shared entries. Include a qualifying narrowing mutant. Do not substitute canonical digest or caller-trusted prose for this concrete relationship. Other object publication/transport boundaries remain outside this finding; no demand is made here to implement all manifest storage or checkpoint publication.\n21|\n22|The recurring family now spans multiple reviews. Route a class-level conformance gate/audit for the owned Session/Lease/Checkpoint relationships before another fixture-only rework. Preserve the complete denominator and the existing closed findings.\n23|\n24|## P2 — Previously qualifying self-predecessor mutant now fails compilation\n25|\n26|`internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py:116` still inserts `return parent, nil`, but CR6 changes checkLeaseChain to return `([]validatedLease, validatedLease, error)`. The anchor still appears once; that proves application only. Running the shipped run() implementation against exact CR6 yields COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE, exit 1, with `lease.go:328:19: not enough return values`. No named behavioral test fails for this plant. The focused battery therefore exits 1.\n27|\n28|Repair this mutation for the new signature while preserving the intended narrow self-link admission and execute its behavioral test. This does not reopen the existing product self-link guard: its current negative tests pass. It repairs newly broken final-source gate evidence. Prior CR5 KILLED evidence cannot establish a compiling plant against the changed signature.\n29|\n30|## Closed CR5 findings and retained bounds\n31|\n32|Independently reran all TestRev5 controls/negatives. Missing required ancestor checkpoint, wrong ancestor session/lease/creator, and wrong winner checkpoint creator now refuse; valid multi-generation and holder controls pass. The original old-plan loss-of-ancestor checkpoint regression passes. These findings are closed.\n33|\n34|Full candidate tests pass, including prior canonical Lease Record identity, lagging replicas, required parked sources, live changed-record refusal, all seven capabilities, predecessor/reducer/enum/crash cases. Earlier architecture and caller integration conclusions remain accepted: CLI invocation, wire Result 5, effects and durable recovery are caller-owned. This read-only API adds no durable mutation protocol. No hosted CI was used.\n35|\n36|## AC coverage\n37|\n38|**8 of 8 AC rows driven at shared production entries; 4 of 8 established and 4 of 8 partial/failing.** Public CLI execution remains the accepted stated bound, 0 of 8 CLI rows delivered by this library leaf.\n39|\n40|| Row | Production entry / named candidate evidence | Result |\n41|| --- | --- | --- |\n42|| UUID/name | Reader.Resolve; TestResolvePinnedPrecedence, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established |\n43|| Qualified selector | Reader.Resolve -> resolveExplicit; TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex, TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures | Established |\n44|| Ambiguity | Reader.Resolve -> matchName/checkRecordAgreement; TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions, TestResolveBareIdentityUnion | Established |\n45|| List summaries | Reader.List/AuthoritativeList -> authorize -> winningLeaseFor; TestSummaryBootstrapRefusals, TestSummaryMixedListRefusesWhole, TestAuthoritativeAdmitsFullCapabilityRegistry | Partial: P1 |\n46|| Status summaries | Reader.AuthoritativeStatus -> authorize -> winningLeaseFor; TestAuthoritativeStatusHealthy, TestAuthoritativeMissingProcessRefusesStatus, TestAuthoritativeHostNameBound64 | Partial: P1 |\n47|| Stable sorting | Reader.List/Resolve; TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity | Established |\n48|| SelectionPlan | Reader.BuildPlan/Revalidate/ParsePlan -> winningLeaseFor; TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts, TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestValidSuccessorBuildsAndRevalidates, TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyRefuses, TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority | Partial: P1 |\n49|| Negative/refusal | Resolve/List/Status/BuildPlan/Revalidate; candidate refusal suites, mutation instrument, reviewer Rev6 test | Partial: P1 and P2 |\n50|\n51|Reviewer Rev6 regressions are attached evidence, not committed candidate tests. Carry them into the producer's next uncommitted candidate.\n52|\n53|## Validation and evidence limits\n54|\n55|Go library, darwin/arm64, Go 1.25.5. Required project-management and architecture-diagrams skills read; main checkout's Curator-managed Go testing skill used because managed links are absent in this Story checkout. No installation.\n56|\n57|- Exact archive `go test ./... -count=1 -v`: exit 0 (`tests.log`); no reviewer TestRev6 in this run.\n58|- Exact archive `go test ./... -cover`: exit 0 (`coverage.log`); sessquery 87.9%, sessrepo 87.2%.\n59|- Exact product plus reviewer test `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev[56]' -count=1 -v`: exit 1 (`probes.log`); all CR5 cases pass, both new invalid variant cases fail, positive controls pass.\n60|- `go build ./...`: exit 0; targeted `go vet ./internal/sessquery ./internal/sessrepo ./internal/provhost`: exit 0. These ran with reviewer test present; product bytes unchanged.\n61|- Exact candidate `gofmt -l internal`: exit 0 with no listed paths (`format-exact.log`). Earlier format.log listed only the unformatted scratch reviewer test, not product code. Producer correctly records old nonexistent cmd/ format command as exit 2, not clean.\n62|- `git diff --check BASE TREE`: exit 0. Local HEAD..main count is 0, recorded only as local ancestry context.\n63|- CR6 publication log independently records exit-0 format/build/full-vet/test/diff commands; this is reused publication evidence, not a new board/race run.\n64|\n65|Operational correction: an initial probe invocation used the active cwd and ran only existing TestRev5 tests, exit 0; its log is retained and excluded from new-probe proof. The first focused mutant copy raced with scratch probe injection, so its control failed on the deliberately failing reviewer test; that run is retained as invalid setup, excluded from mutation classifications. The corrected focused run uses exact candidate source without reviewer injection. No failure is relabeled passing.\n66|\n67|The attached evidence bundle includes exact-tree path hashes, reviewer tests, actual logs, focused script retaining the shipped run() body/plants, final mutation classifications, and producer focused logs. Prior CR5 review evidence was materialized and read; unchanged closed audits are reused with the above bounds rather than repeated wholesale. Acceptance remains withheld; route to-dev, not blocked, integrating or done.\n68|\n69|Final independent focused mutation result: **3 KILLED (new narrowing plants), 1 SURVIVED (applied harmless comment), 1 COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE (N-chain-self), 2 CONTROL exit 0; overall exit 1**. Raw logs and mutants.json are in mutants-exact/. This is a focused selection of shipped plants with the identical run() implementation, not a claimed rerun of the entire historical battery.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c425","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0892e-c94e-7771-b9cd-b99166499f5d"},"sequence":109,"recorded_at":1780531400000213,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2"},"call_id":"call_01a0892f07d970c097f2c62d690a2521","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-21gygk/TASK-260830-21gygk_results-rev6.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-21gygk — rev6 rework outcome (rev5 verdict changes-requested)\n2|\n3|Producer rework for `TASK-260830-21gygk_review-verdict-rev5.md` (CR5 tree\n4|`ab3a8894386128681aa4e9dce451cb43c261db3e`, base `8cf4aaa...`, story\n5|checkpoint `83640d191f78f0cd685e5f709027819799efe1cf`). Both P1 findings\n6|are fixed on the shared semantic admission path. Candidate left\n7|UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for CR snapshotting; no branch\n8|mutation, no integration, no hosted CI.\n9|\n10|## Failing baseline (pre-fix, ported reviewer regressions)\n11|\n12|Copied `/tmp/rev5ev/reviewer_rev5_test.go` to\n13|`internal/sessquery/rev5_regression_test.go` and ran before any\n14|production change (`go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev5'`):\n15|\n16|- `TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority/missing_ancestor_checkpoint`\n17|  FAIL: BuildPlan admitted, Revalidate(old plan and new) nil,\n18|  AuthoritativeStatus/List admitted.\n19|- `TestRev5CheckpointCreatorMustBeHolder/non_holder` FAIL: all four\n20|  entries admitted.\n21|- Both `complete`/`holder` positive controls PASSED.\n22|- Raw log: worktree `.temp/rev5-failing-baseline.log` (ignored scratch).\n23|\n24|## Production fix (`internal/sessquery/lease.go` only)\n25|\n26|- `validatedCheckpoint` gains `CreatorHostID`; `parseCheckpointRecord`\n27|  parses `created_by_host_id` as UUIDv7 (`invalid_config` when malformed).\n28|- `checkLeaseChain` now returns the winner-to-root ancestry chain in\n29|  addition to the direct predecessor (walk semantics unchanged).\n30|- `checkWinnerCheckpoint` additionally enforces checkpoint creator ==\n31|  owning lease holder (predecessor holder at epoch > 1, self at epoch 1).\n32|- New `checkAncestorCheckpoints` + `checkCheckpointBinding` validate\n33|  every non-winner lease of the winning ancestry: epoch > 1 must\n34|  reference an admitted checkpoint for its session and predecessor\n35|  lease with creator == predecessor holder; the epoch-1 root may omit\n36|  the reference, otherwise it must bind to itself with creator == its\n37|  holder. Unresolvable/misbound references refuse\n38|  `selector_observation_unavailable`. Only the winner's ancestry is\n39|  consulted, so legal branching, lagging copies, canonical identity,\n40|  and parked-source refusal are preserved.\n41|- `winningLeaseFor` (shared by BuildPlan/bindPlan, Revalidate,\n42|  authorize/AuthoritativeStatus/AuthoritativeList) runs all three\n43|  checks, so old-plan invalidation after loss of ancestor checkpoint\n44|  falls out of the same gate.\n45|\n46|## Committed tests\n47|\n48|- Ported reviewer tests kept in `internal/sessquery/rev5_regression_test.go`.\n49|- Added `TestRev5AncestorCheckpointBinding` (wrong-session, wrong-lease,\n50|  wrong-creator ancestor checkpoints, each through BuildPlan,\n51|  Revalidate, AuthoritativeStatus, AuthoritativeList) with shared\n52|  `rev5AncestorFixture` 3-generation control.\n53|- Post-fix: `go test ./internal/sessquery -run '^TestRev5'` — all pass.\n54|\n55|## Narrowing mutants (focused battery, same instrument as committed `testdata/mutate.py`)\n56|\n57|Driver + raw logs + manifest: worktree\n58|`.temp/TASK-260830-21gygk/mutants-rev5/` (ignored scratch;\n59|`mutants-rev5.json` manifest, per-plant `.log` files with real exits).\n60|Each plant keeps the gate and admits exactly one member; files restored\n61|with digest verification; controls green.\n62|\n63|| Mutant | Classification | Killed by |\n64|| --- | --- | --- |\n65|| N-ancestor-checkpoint (skip leaseB ancestor) | KILLED (exit 1) | TestRev5AncestorCheckpointAuthority(/missing...), TestRev5AncestorCheckpointBinding(/wrong_session/wrong_lease/wrong_creator) |\n66|| N-checkpoint-holder (admit hostB creator, winner path) | KILLED (exit 1) | TestRev5CheckpointCreatorMustBeHolder(/non_holder) |\n67|| N-ancestor-holder (admit hostB creator, ancestor path) | KILLED (exit 1) | TestRev5AncestorCheckpointBinding(/wrong_creator) |\n68|| C-harmless-comment | SURVIVED (exit 0, applied log) | control — behavior-preserving |\n69|| control-before / control-after | CONTROL exit 0 | — |\n70|\n71|The two holder plants kill disjoint test sets, proving the two guard\n72|sites are distinct and both required. The same three plants were added\n73|to the committed `internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py` battery; every\n74|lease.go anchor in the full battery counts exactly 1 occurrence in the\n75|final source (N-chain-self, N-checkpoint-placeholder, N-lease-missing,\n76|C-harmless-comment, plus the 3 new).\n77|\n78|## Validation (all observed this run)\n79|\n80|- `go build ./...` — exit 0.\n81|- `go vet ./internal/sessquery/ ./internal/sessrepo/ ./internal/provhost/` — exit 0.\n82|- `gofmt -l internal/` — clean, no files listed. NOTE correcting the\n83|  prior evidence description: the old `validation-final.log` gofmt\n84|  failure was exit 2 because it passed a nonexistent `cmd/` directory;\n85|  the valid command is `gofmt -l internal/` (no `cmd/` exists in repo).\n86|- `git diff --check -- internal/ README.md` — exit 0.\n87|- `go test ./... -count=1` — all packages ok (sessquery, sessrepo,\n88|  sessstate, provhost, canonicaljson, specdoc, traceability, etc.).\n89|- Coverage: sessquery 87.9%, sessrepo 87.2% of statements.\n90|- No durable writes on these paths (read-only selector leaf); no\n91|  crash/idempotency protocol change — retained creation-crash\n92|  composition tests still green.\n93|\n94|## Docs / traceability\n95|\n96|- `README.md` and `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`\n97|  (\"fully validated succession\") now state whole-ancestry plus holder\n98|  binding; TRACEABILITY row 45 names the new tests and mutants.\n99|- `LOGBOOK.md` carries the rev6 rework entry.\n100|\n101|## AC coverage: 8 of 8 rows driven through shared production entries\n102|\n103|Reader.Resolve (UUID/name: TestResolvePinnedPrecedence,\n104|TestResolveBareIdentityUnion; qualified: TestResolveQualifiedSourcesSelectOneIndex,\n105|TestResolveQualifiedSourceNeverFallsBack, TestResolveExplicitSourceReadFailures;\n106|ambiguity: TestResolveExactNamesAndASCIICollisions; sorting:\n107|TestListStatusDerivedFactsAndStableOrder, TestResolvePeerOrderAndReplicatedIdentity),\n108|Reader.BuildPlan/Revalidate/ParsePlan (TestBuildPlanBindsCurrentFacts,\n109|TestRevalidateDetectsEachFactChange, TestValidSuccessorBuildsAndRevalidates,\n110|TestRevalidateUnionParkedCopyRefuses + rev5 ancestry/holder suites),\n111|Reader.AuthoritativeStatus/List (TestAuthoritativeStatusHealthy,\n112|TestAuthoritativeMissingProcessRefusesStatus,\n113|TestAuthoritativeHostNameBound64, TestAuthoritativeAdmitsFullCapabilityRegistry\n114|+ rev5 suites through both entries). Public CLI execution remains the\n115|stated caller-integration bound (0 CLI rows in this leaf).\n116|\n117|## Candidate paths (uncommitted, Story worktree)\n118|\n119|- `internal/sessquery/lease.go` (fix)\n120|- `internal/sessquery/rev5_regression_test.go` (ported + new tests)\n121|- `internal/sessquery/testdata/mutate.py` (3 narrowing plants)\n122|- `internal/sessquery/TRACEABILITY.md`, `README.md`, `LOGBOOK.md` (docs)\n123|- Retained prior CR5 scope untouched (sessrepo checkpoint/lease owners,\n124|  provhost/sessrepo test updates).\n125|- No stray `--help`/mutation-source tree in the candidate diff;\n126|  mutant scratch lives under ignored `.temp/` only.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
