{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca9f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0892e-c94e-7771-b9cd-b99166499f5d"},"sequence":938,"recorded_at":1780531400001871,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a08931-2364-7a72-b086-c1b533d21011"},"task_id":"01a08931-2364-7a72-b086-c1b533d21011","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a08931-2364-7a72-b086-c1b533d21011","chunk":"Read text file `internal/sessstate/doc.go`.\n1|// Package sessstate derives deterministic logical-session state from\n2|// immutable records according to AX v0.5.0 Sections 2.3, 5.1-5.2, 5.7,\n3|// and 14.4: every SessionState value, the winning lease epoch, lease\n4|// conflicts, the current checkpoint, provider identity, and terminal\n5|// binding.\n6|//\n7|// The reducer is a pure function of its input: Reduce takes decoded\n8|// record and event facts and returns one Projection. It performs no\n9|// I/O, reads no clock, and keeps no cache, so the same event sequence\n10|// always yields the same state. Project binds the pure core to a\n11|// sessrepo.Repository for one session: it loads the stored record and\n12|// the authoritative chain through the repository's production entries\n13|// and folds them through Reduce. Project only reads; it mutates no\n14|// durable state of its own and owns no crash window.\n15|//\n16|// Division of authority inside this story:\n17|//\n18|//   - Durable session state — the immutable record, the ordered event\n19|//     chain, source sequence continuity, and the per-session parked\n20|//     channel — is owned by internal/sessrepo and reached only through\n21|//     its production entries (ListSessions, GetRecord, ListEvents,\n22|//     GetEvent). This package never decodes a chain index, never\n23|//     attests a blob, and never lists a session directory.\n24|//   - Canonical attestation stays single-owned: identity, the closed\n25|//     Session Record and Session Event shapes, the per-type payload\n26|//     union, and the unknown-v1-type inert rule are verified by\n27|//     internal/canonicaljson at the sessrepo durable boundary only.\n28|//     The provhost no-attestation-outside-the-leaf gate pins that\n29|//     exclusivity, so Decode projects members from attested bytes and\n30|//     never re-verifies. The payload members Reduce reads were\n31|//     admitted by that closed shape, and a member that no longer\n32|//     decodes refuses the derivation instead of reading as absent.\n33|//   - Strict frame decoding and scalar bound checks stay with their\n34|//     owners: environ.DecodeStrictObject for the JSON frame,\n35|//     environ.CheckUUIDv7 and environ.CheckUint53Bounds for identifier\n36|//     and counter members, scalar.ParseDigest and scalar.ParseUUIDv4\n37|//     for digest and UUID grammars (UUIDv7 members stay with\n38|//     environ.CheckUUIDv7, which owns that check),\n39|//     scalar.ParseProviderID for the provider alphabet, and\n40|//     terminalbackend.ParseID for the terminal backend alphabet.\n41|//   - The refusal census denominator is derived from production\n42|//     through internal/invcore; see census_test.go.\n43|//\n44|// A parked session from sessrepo reaches SessionState as a state, not\n45|// as an error or an omission: when ListSessions reports Parked for the\n46|// session, Project returns a parked Projection carrying the blocking\n47|// reason and the retry hint, and Reduce folds an explicit Parked input\n48|// the same way. A name that exists but is parked still resolves as not\n49|// found at the sessrepo entry; Project takes a session UUID, and the\n50|// listing distinguishes a parked session (entry present) from an\n51|// unknown one (entry absent), so no sessrepo interface change is\n52|// needed for this leaf.\n53|//\n54|// Stated bounds (not silent gaps):\n55|//\n56|//   - Single authoritative chain. Reduce folds exactly the events it\n57|//     is given in order and re-checks chain continuity itself, so a\n58|//     chain-forbidden reordering refuses instead of silently deriving\n59|//     a different state. Cross-partition lease convergence beyond the\n60|//     tuple rule belongs to the ownership-leases story: competing\n61|//     off-chain leases enter only through Input.Union, and the union\n62|//     never rewrites authoritative state — it selects the reported\n63|//     winner and records conflicts.\n64|//   - No name resolution, no list/status rendering, no peer names, and\n65|//     no interactive choice: the local sessrepo steps are reused\n66|//     through Project's listing lookup, and the full Section 2.3 order\n67|//     with choice plus Section 14.4 rendering belong to the sibling\n68|//     name-resolution leaf that builds on this projection.\n69|//   - No persisted profile derivation. Section 2.4 effective-profile\n70|//     authority is out of this leaf's scoped sections; profile.changed\n71|//     and the profile pairs on launch, resume, and fork events are\n72|//     retained as inert facts.\n73|//   - No execution-realm readiness, workspace materialization status,\n74|//     capability map, or sync-age derivation: those Section 14.4\n75|//     fields belong to the provider, workspace, and mesh leaves. The\n76|//     warnings member carries only what this leaf derives\n77|//     (divergent history, stale process, parked blocking reason).\n78|//   - Local role derives from a caller-supplied local host ID against\n79|//     the owner host of the newest authoritative event. An empty local\n80|//     host ID leaves the role unknown rather than guessing replica.\n81|//   - An empty chain derives creating with no authoritative lease, but\n82|//     the union is still validated and resolves the reported winner\n83|//     through the same resolveWinner path: a malformed union refuses\n84|//     exactly as on a non-empty chain, while a well-formed union moves\n85|//     only the reported winner (with its named conflict) and never\n86|//     rewrites the creating state. Local is ignored on this path, including\n87|//     malformed and partial tuples: without an authoritative event there is\n88|//     no local process lease to fence or owner host to compare. LocalHostID\n89|//     leaves the role unknown, even when Union reports a winner. No Local\n90|//     validation is claimed. TestReduceEmptyChainLocalIsIgnored pins this\n91|//     bound through Reduce with and without a selected union winner.\n92|//\n93|// The package adds no ax command, no doctor result, and no runtime\n94|// capability claim.\n95|package sessstate","final_result":true}}}
