{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cd7f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0892e-c94e-7771-b9cd-b99166499f5d"},"sequence":1306,"recorded_at":1780531400002607,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2"},"call_id":"call_01a089333ea1756385ac6789707be856","text":"Read text file `internal/sessquery/lease.go`.\n(317 line(s) above)\n318|// historical heads stay admissible and are never required to equal\n319|// the current tail. Absence refuses observation_unavailable; a\n320|// lease above epoch 1 without its named predecessor in the admitted\n321|// set refuses the same class rather than binding a dangling\n322|// successor, while an illegal predecessor link is malformed\n323|// authority (integrity failure).\n324|func (reader *Reader) winningLeaseFor(sessionID, sessionKind string, repo *sessrepo.Repository) (validatedLease, error) {\n325|\tif sessionKind != \"direct\" && sessionKind != \"task_board\" {\n326|\t\treturn validatedLease{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: session %s carries unknown kind %q for checkpoint persistence\", ErrInvalidConfig, sessionID, sessionKind)\n327|\t}\n328|\tbySession, err := reader.validatedLeasesBySession()\n329|\tif err != nil {\n330|\t\treturn validatedLease{}, err\n331|\t}\n332|\tcandidates := bySession[sessionID]\n333|\tif len(candidates) == 0 {\n334|\t\treturn validatedLease{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: winning lease record for session %s cannot be established\", ErrObservationUnavailable, sessionID)\n335|\t}\n336|\twinner := candidates[0]\n337|\tfor _, candidate := range candidates[1:] {\n338|\t\tif sessstate.Compare(\n339|\t\t\tsessstate.LeaseHead{Epoch: candidate.Epoch, LeaseID: candidate.LeaseID},\n340|\t\t\tsessstate.LeaseHead{Epoch: winner.Epoch, LeaseID: winner.LeaseID},\n341|\t\t) > 0 {\n342|\t\t\twinner = candidate\n343|\t\t}\n344|\t}\n345|\tchain, predecessor, err := checkLeaseChain(candidates, winner)\n346|\tif err != nil {\n347|\t\treturn validatedLease{}, err\n348|\t}\n349|\tif err := reader.checkWinnerCheckpoint(winner, predecessor, sessionKind); err != nil {\n350|\t\treturn validatedLease{}, err\n351|\t}\n352|\tif err := reader.checkAncestorCheckpoints(chain, sessionKind); err != nil {\n353|\t\treturn validatedLease{}, err\n354|\t}\n355|\treturn winner, nil\n356|}\n357|\n358|// checkLeaseChain validates the winner's predecessor ancestry within\n359|// the admitted records for its session. Section 5.3 requires every\n360|// epoch above 1 to name a known predecessor for the same session\n361|// with an epoch exactly one below, down to an epoch-1 root with a\n362|// null predecessor; epochs below 1 cannot exist, so an epoch-1\n363|// lease naming any predecessor is malformed. A self, cyclic,\n364|// skipped, contradictory, or duplicated link is malformed authority\n365|// (integrity failure); a missing predecessor name or record is\n366|// incomplete authority (observation_unavailable). Epochs strictly\n367|// decrease along the walk, so the walk always terminates. It\n368|// returns the winning ancestry from the winner down to the epoch-1\n369|// root, plus the winner's direct predecessor, or the zero lease at\n370|// epoch 1.\n371|func checkLeaseChain(candidates []validatedLease, winner validatedLease) ([]validatedLease, validatedLease, error) {\n372|\tbyLease := make(map[string]validatedLease, len(candidates))\n373|\tfor _, candidate := range candidates {\n374|\t\tif previous, ok := byLease[candidate.LeaseID]; ok && previous.Digest != candidate.Digest {\n375|\t\t\treturn nil, validatedLease{}, fmt.Errorf(\"%w: session %s carries contradictory lease records for lease %s\", sessstate.ErrIntegrity, winner.SessionID, candidate.LeaseID)\n376|\t\t}\n377|\t\tbyLease[candidate.LeaseID] = candidate\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
