{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000da4b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0892e-c94e-7771-b9cd-b99166499f5d"},"sequence":2944,"recorded_at":1780531400005883,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"23d6464a-2d0b-430c-994a-f34a5b1772f2"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0893c-7371-75f3-a2be-d338e2e645f2"},"task_id":"01a0893c-7371-75f3-a2be-d338e2e645f2","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0893c-7371-75f3-a2be-d338e2e645f2","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(1859 line(s) above)\n1860|- Immutable plans: `Reader.BuildPlan` binds all sixteen §14.7.2\n1861|  members — the literal selector, session and validated record digest,\n1862|  source host (always a UUIDv7; a local selection without a known local\n1863|  host refuses `invalid_config`) and exact alias, index and\n1864|  configuration digests, the validated winning `urn:ax:schema:lease`\n1865|  Lease Record digest with its epoch, lease ID, and holder from that\n1866|  same record (admitted through the canonicaljson owner from\n1867|  `Reader.LeaseRecords`, greatest (epoch, lease_id) winner with a\n1868|  fully validated succession: the predecessor ancestry chains by\n1869|  epoch plus one to an epoch-1 null-predecessor root, and every\n1870|  lease in that winning ancestry above epoch 1 references an\n1871|  admitted `urn:ax:schema:checkpoint` Checkpoint Record from\n1872|  `Reader.CheckpointRecords` for its session and predecessor lease,\n1873|  each created by the owning lease holder and each carrying the\n1874|  persistence variant the referenced Session Record kind selects\n1875|  (direct only provider-manifest, task_board only task-board-bundle;\n1876|  §5.4); no envelope\n1877|  observation substitutes for it),\n1878|  lease/event/tombstone authority heads (winning lease digest plus\n1879|  every non-parked source tail, sorted unique), action, destination,\n1880|  and expectation digest. A session with no admitted winning record\n1881|  refuses `selector_observation_unavailable`; a complete read proving\n1882|  a record without any valid lease refuses\n1883|  `selector_bootstrap_incomplete` instead of binding an empty triple.\n1884|  `Reader.Revalidate` compares every bound fact in a fixed order and\n1885|  validates the complete authority union for the pinned UUID across\n1886|  the local and every allowlisted source — contradictory records are\n1887|  `integrity_failure`, a greater winning lease and fresh tombstone\n1888|  evidence are `selector_plan_stale` while lagging copies stay\n1889|  current, and a parked copy of the pinned session in any required\n1890|  source fails the union closed with\n1891|  `selector_observation_unavailable` (never evidence, never absence)\n1892|  — without re-resolving names or substituting selections.\n1893|  Revocation is `peer_not_allowlisted`, and reads keep their classes.\n1894|  Plans authorize read projection only; fencing, commit, and remote\n1895|  routes belong to the CLI/lifecycle callers that invoke revalidation.\n1896|\n1897|`Reader.List` and `Reader.Status` read actual Session Records and event\n1898|chains through `sessrepo` and `sessstate.Projector`. They expose the\n1899|derived identity, provider, lifecycle, winning lease/owner, local role,\n1900|checkpoint ID, conflicts, and warnings as an internal `Summary`. List\n1901|order is bytewise session ID; `InspectLocal` retains raw access to\n1902|parked/tombstoned IDs and recovery diagnostics and is not a public\n1903|summary entry. Failed index reads and failed projections propagate as\n1904|errors. Repository-parked sessions remain visible in listing but are\n1905|excluded from live routing. Reading never repairs a store or performs\n1906|an attach, resume, or ownership change. Creating is a record AND an\n1907|authoritative initial lease (§5.7/§13.1 step 2), so a record-only chain\n1908|is an interrupted prefix for the bootstrap-recovery leaf: list and\n1909|status refuse it with `selector_bootstrap_incomplete` — the whole list\n1910|when any encountered record is unrepresentable — instead of returning\n1911|an ownerless row or a placeholder owner. The closed authoritative\n1912|layer (`Reader.AuthoritativeStatus`, `Reader.AuthoritativeList`)\n1913|binds owner, lease, and role from the validated winning Lease Record,\n1914|owner display names only from validated host metadata (1..64), local\n1915|roles only with a known local host, checkpoint timestamps only from\n1916|validated observations, workspace_status from the closed five-value\n1917|enum, capabilities from validated CapabilitySummary maps (0..7, only\n1918|available may enable) keyed by exactly the provhost-owned Section 7.3\n1919|seven-name provider registry (any other name refuses\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
